{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"a706cb9b93c3c7e7","type":"group","x":1900,"y":100,"width":2260,"height":1340,"color":"1","label":"Tutorial"},
		{"id":"bbee386f60e2b60c","type":"group","x":20,"y":100,"width":1750,"height":1580,"label":"The Human Who Pushed Buttons"},
		{"id":"more","type":"text","text":"Could there be MORE to this story?\n---\nCould there be hidden depths burried far below what meets the eye?","x":-800,"y":2100,"width":300,"height":200,"color":"0"},
		{"id":"options","type":"text","text":"⚙️ Options\n---\nWIP: Some buttons are part of the INTERFACE at the top of your screen. They'll appear one by one with context. Obviously a light/dark mode toggle.\n  Include a jab about language 🇬🇧 apologize for it being english only but the html structure is dead simple so translation tools should work. Add an aside to explain that websites used to have automated translation but that got out of fashion when google got monopoly over chrome.\n  Make sure to include plenty of accessibility options for gamers.","x":4640,"y":280,"width":300,"height":200,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"tutorial","type":"text","text":"❓ What do I have to do?\n---\nYour GOAL is simple: find an ending flag 🏁.\n  There's an ending 🏁 at the end of the green 🟢 line.\n  There may be others.","x":2480,"y":120,"width":300,"height":200,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"more2","type":"text","text":"Could there be an orange button drowned in a sea of grey?\n---\nThat is when the human found a story.\n  It laid there, shining green, in the middle of all the buttons.\n  It was story left untold, almost forgotten.\n  And its title was...","x":-800,"y":2360,"width":300,"height":200,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"intro_grey","type":"text","text":"Some buttons were grey.","x":20,"y":420,"width":300,"height":60,"color":"0"},
		{"id":"intro_draw","type":"text","text":"Some buttons drew more buttons.","x":240,"y":568,"width":300,"height":72,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"intro_green","type":"text","text":"Some buttons were green.","x":350,"y":420,"width":300,"height":60,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"end_flag","type":"text","text":"🏁 And so it came to be that the human stopped pushing buttons.\n---","x":540,"y":1420,"width":300,"height":200,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"warning","type":"text","text":"⚠️ Content warning\n---\nThis games contains a lot of button pushing, and a lot of TEXT including METAPHORS and ALLEGORIES.\n  It discusses sensitive topics such as colors, HISTORY, SLAVERY, INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY, WIP...\n  No topic is ever approached without a suitable warning in the unpressed button text.\n  Never forget who is pushing the buttons.\n  Reader discretion is advised when pushing buttons.","x":5040,"y":0,"width":300,"height":200,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"tuto_colors","type":"text","text":"❓ What's up with the colors?\n---\nWIP: Buttons have colors, you can see how many you got in this menu. This is meant to help people track progress. maybe i'll add completion rates at the bottom though its hard in HTML 🎨","x":2780,"y":920,"width":300,"height":200,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"tuto_apology","type":"text","text":"❓ This tutorial is too long!\n---\nI apologize, this is brand new game engine, a lot of things need to be explained.\n  Feel free to skip everything you want, or look at the ⚙️ options to customize your experience.","x":2370,"y":1220,"width":300,"height":200,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"tuto_archive","type":"text","text":"❓ Help, my screen is full of stuff!\n---\nWIP: The thread 🧵 button helps navigate between open threads. The 🗑️ button will give you options to cleanup READ messages. 💾 there will be a save management file to allow EASY sync between different devices/different scenarii of the game engine maybe","x":2440,"y":960,"width":300,"height":200,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"tuto_emoji","type":"text","text":"❓ What's up with the EMOJIs?\n---\nSome buttons have icons.\n  WIP: You can collect them in this menu ☺️. There might be other quests 🏆 (find names 👥, places 📍, times ⏰, maybe rare collectibles 🐟)","x":2020,"y":980,"width":300,"height":200,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"title_aside","type":"text","text":"The story of a white man?\n---\nAlas, that is where we must start.\n  Humans do love their stories to be character-centered.\n  But fear not, you will see many characters if you press the right buttons.","x":900,"y":2920,"width":300,"height":200,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"e8a4775851bc5327","type":"text","text":"📷 That's not the title of the book, though...\n---\nIts original title was:\n\"The\nLIFE\nand\nStrange Surprizing \nADVENTURES\nof \nRobinson Crusoe\nof York, Mariner:\n\nWho lived Eight and Twenty Years, all alone in an un-inhabited Island on the Coast of America, near the Mouth of the Great River of Oroonoque;\nHaving been cast on Shore by Shipwreck, wherein all the Men perished but himself. \n\nWITH\nAn Account how he was at last as strangely deliver'd by Pyrates. \nWritten by Himself.\"\n\nYou can see it for yourself on <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Robinson_Crusoe_1719_1st_edition.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Wikimedia.\n<img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1e/Robinson_Crusoe_1719_1st_edition.jpg\" /></a>","x":1140,"y":3630,"width":440,"height":460,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"d59c4d2f4f4674df","type":"text","text":"Strange surprizing adventures...\n---\nLike the one you're living right now!","x":1720,"y":4160,"width":260,"height":140,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"start","type":"text","text":"⭐ Start\n---\nThis game is about buttons.\n  Buttons have two states: pushed and not pushed.\n  When you FIRST click on them, they EXPAND and draw other buttons.","x":360,"y":-320,"width":300,"height":200,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"beginning","type":"text","text":"⭐ The Human Who Pushed Buttons\n---\nThere once was a human, who pushed buttons.","x":390,"y":120,"width":300,"height":200,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"72d5074d19b63713","type":"text","text":"You forgot the part at the bottom...","x":2340,"y":4160,"width":300,"height":80,"color":"0"},
		{"id":"ed26200129d229b8","type":"text","text":"👥 Printed for W. Taylor","x":2290,"y":4300,"width":230,"height":100,"color":"0"},
		{"id":"99677d0088771e0d","type":"text","text":"📍 at the Shop in Pater-Noster-Row","x":2560,"y":4300,"width":200,"height":120,"color":"0"},
		{"id":"intro_orange","type":"text","text":"Some buttons were orange.","x":1430,"y":420,"width":300,"height":60,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"intro_blue","type":"text","text":"Some buttons were blue.","x":690,"y":420,"width":300,"height":60,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"intro_purple","type":"text","text":"Some buttons were purple.","x":1070,"y":420,"width":300,"height":60,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"intro_draw3","type":"text","text":"It was always a surprise to push buttons and wonder what would happen next.","x":400,"y":720,"width":300,"height":120,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"found_flag","type":"text","text":"One day, while pushing buttons, the human came accross an ending flag 🏁.\n---\nThis puzzled the human quite a bit. An ending flag 🏁 ? So soon?","x":400,"y":1160,"width":300,"height":200,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"intro_draw2","type":"text","text":"Some buttons did not draw more buttons.","x":590,"y":568,"width":300,"height":72,"color":"0"},
		{"id":"intro_draw4","type":"text","text":"And so the human kept pushing buttons.\n---\nThe human pushed buttons by day,\n  The human pushed buttons by night.\n  So much so that the human's life was mostly pushing buttons.\n  But the human had to keep pushing.\n  How else would the human live?","x":400,"y":900,"width":300,"height":200,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"tuto_star","type":"text","text":"❓ What does the star ⭐ mean ?\n---\nStar ⭐ is the icon for starter packs. They mark the beginning of a story.","x":2880,"y":480,"width":300,"height":160,"color":"0"},
		{"id":"02b8cc538f2e9888","type":"text","text":"❓ This thing is new kind of game engine?\n---\nA new medium?\nA new way to see?\nA new way to LOOK.","x":3200,"y":480,"width":360,"height":180,"color":"2"},
		{
			"id":"894d8e9bcd6407da",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"What the *** is a green?\n---\nYou know? The <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Village_green\" target=\"_blank\">greens</a>! From the inclosures!",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-2270,
			"y":6760,
			"width":420,
			"height":120,
			"color":"5"
		},
		{
			"id":"3c15c4f2632c1045",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"So... the author of Robinson Crusoe had no actual travel experience?\n---\nWell, it would appear so.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-3290,
			"y":6545,
			"width":260,
			"height":185,
			"color":"2"
		},
		{
			"id":"82457e74613347a6",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"🚢 Travel, you say?\n---\nThere is no historical record of Daniel Defoe ever setting foot outside the British Isles.\nThere are however a lot of mentions of him being an avid armchair traveler.\nHe would read everything he came across when it came to international travel.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-3160,
			"y":6050,
			"width":300,
			"height":320,
			"color":"6"
		},
		{
			"id":"473213a9261ef550",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"A famous religious and intellectual microcosm for Dissenters.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-2560,
			"y":6390,
			"width":260,
			"height":190
		},
		{
			"id":"9e51b34e90f4962c",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Newington Green is a district in the North of London\n---\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newington_Green",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-2860,
			"y":5700,
			"width":430,
			"height":140
		},
		{
			"id":"e1aff5886c20bec7",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The school was shut down due to religious pressure when Defoe was a young adult.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-2470,
			"y":5590,
			"width":420,
			"height":80
		},
		{
			"id":"061ca5ebd5e9bf0f",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"👥 Charles Morton\n---\nA pioneer intellectual who revolutionized education.\nHe ran a private academy for 20 years before moving to America.\nHe went on to have a major role in the founding of Harvard University.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-2790,
			"y":5940,
			"width":360,
			"height":220
		},
		{
			"id":"8676648ae26bcd81",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"💼 During his early life, Daniel Defoe was a travelling salesman.\n---\nHe rode thousands of miles all across England and Scotland.\nHe dealt in stockings (wool, silk, and cotton), but also branched out into wine, spirits, and tobacco.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-3700,
			"y":5670,
			"width":470,
			"height":210,
			"color":"4"
		},
		{
			"id":"239181232a3195da",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"📍 Does the school building remain?\n---\nThe building did not survive the test of time, but \n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?client=firefox-b-d&q=Charles+Morton+Court\" target=\"_blank\">Charles Morton Court Prestige Student Housing</a> serve as a testament to its legacy.\nIn 2026, it seems to stand above a \"Papa Johns\" and a \"Tesco Express\".\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/place/Prestige+Student+Living+Charles+Morton+Court/@51.5527125,-0.0872473,3a,75y,208.91h,112.2t/data=!3m7!1e1!3m5!1sO7GHLRfen4fRk_ZkWiYi4A!2e0!6shttps:%2F%2Fstreetviewpixels-pa.googleapis.com%2Fv1%2Fthumbnail%3Fcb_client%3Dmaps_sv.tactile%26w%3D900%26h%3D600%26pitch%3D-22.199785617299767%26panoid%3DO7GHLRfen4fRk_ZkWiYi4A%26yaw%3D208.90594074437794!7i16384!8i8192!4m6!3m5!1s0x48761c86b08c46fb:0xd1ae95b42a8e4ec0!8m2!3d51.5526405!4d-0.0873502!16s%2Fg%2F1vvr5q51?entry=ttu&g_ep=EgoyMDI2MDQyOS4wIKXMDSoASAFQAw%3D%3D\" target=\"_blank\">Here is Street View and Google Maps reviews.</a>\n<iframe src=\"https://www.google.com/maps/place/Prestige+Student+Living+Charles+Morton+Court/@51.5527125,-0.0872473,3a,75y,208.91h,112.2t/data=!3m7!1e1!3m5!1sO7GHLRfen4fRk_ZkWiYi4A!2e0!6shttps:%2F%2Fstreetviewpixels-pa.googleapis.com%2Fv1%2Fthumbnail%3Fcb_client%3Dmaps_sv.tactile%26w%3D900%26h%3D600%26pitch%3D-22.199785617299767%26panoid%3DO7GHLRfen4fRk_ZkWiYi4A%26yaw%3D208.90594074437794!7i16384!8i8192!4m6!3m5!1s0x48761c86b08c46fb:0xd1ae95b42a8e4ec0!8m2!3d51.5526405!4d-0.0873502!16s%2Fg%2F1vvr5q51?entry=ttu&g_ep=EgoyMDI2MDQyOS4wIKXMDSoASAFQAw%3D%3D\"></iframe>",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-2250,
			"y":6140,
			"width":400,
			"height":440,
			"color":"6"
		},
		{
			"id":"18924d63f3bc5fa5",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"💸 They made it!\n---\nThey were \"New Money\".\nThe American dream...",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-2170,
			"y":5035,
			"width":260,
			"height":145,
			"color":"6"
		},
		{
			"id":"f9a56dfc6bb04b2e",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The best education money could buy?\n---\nBack in those days, the standard prestigious institutions like Oxford or Cambridge required religious oath to the English religion, which some, like Daniel Defoe's family refused to take.\n\nInstead, they formed privately financed and operated so-called \"Dissenter\" academies, private boarding school which rapidly surpassed the old establishments in the technologies they could afford.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-2000,
			"y":5590,
			"width":420,
			"height":360,
			"color":"5"
		},
		{
			"id":"21687949a41e78bc",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Daniel Defoe studied in Charles Morton’s Academy at Newington Green\n--\nIt was a brand new kind of education.\nThe best money could buy.\nIt was a very progressive education focused on knowledge for the sake of doing.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-3280,
			"y":5108,
			"width":480,
			"height":245
		},
		{
			"id":"fd8affe066a584ff",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"What happened to them after the return of the monarchy?\n---\nThey had to keep their faith secret since it was illegal.\nThousands fled to America. Most stayed.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1730,
			"y":7165,
			"width":420,
			"height":180,
			"color":"5"
		},
		{
			"id":"fec336acff3f8ceb",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# What's a Dissenter\n---\nAs opposed to Conformists, Dissenters are catholic protestants who refuse the English monarch as \"pope\".\nA lot of them were in some ways refugees from the continent fleeing persecution.\nSome were of French or Flemish origins.\nThey were the religious movement underpinning the republican revolution a decade earlier, and the puritan dictatorship that succeeded.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1700,
			"y":6580,
			"width":420,
			"height":360,
			"color":"5"
		},
		{
			"id":"4c31c73f1f9710ad",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Wealthy bourgeois merchants, religious extremists, fallen from power...\n---\nAnd hungry for revenge?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1360,
			"y":6985,
			"width":460,
			"height":150,
			"color":"2"
		},
		{
			"id":"7ed03c78122433b8",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Daniel Defoe received the closest thing to an MBA that existed in the 17th century.\n---\nMathematics and languages as business tools.\nWith a heavy dose of religious and ethical leaning.\n",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-900,
			"y":6455,
			"width":340,
			"height":260
		},
		{
			"id":"9545fa71db756f1a",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"They taught that the \"Flow of Goods\" was God’s way of bringing the world together.\n---\nProperty Rights and Contract Law were nearly as sacred as the Ten Commandments.\n\nThis gave Defoe a lifelong obsession with the \"Dignity of Trade.\"",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-850,
			"y":6815,
			"width":360,
			"height":320,
			"color":"2"
		},
		{
			"id":"cc2c941236c1540a",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Do I smell the distinctive odor of business school?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-840,
			"y":6315,
			"width":260,
			"height":60,
			"color":"6"
		},
		{
			"id":"1364f5e6e7a345df",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"So Daniel Defoe grew up in a cultish microcosm? \n---\nHe did live in rebel, dissentious districts. ",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1330,
			"y":7465,
			"width":360,
			"height":160,
			"color":"6"
		},
		{
			"id":"531817bb5f8b90ca",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Dignity?\n---\nAs opposed to the \"decadent\" birthright aristocracy.\nToo complacent.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-830,
			"y":7315,
			"width":320,
			"height":160,
			"color":"4"
		},
		{
			"id":"0a424ad760b7b70b",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"✝️ The protestant work ethic?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":230,
			"y":7255,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"adc2ce5c16579335",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"🚰 I hope you have a source for that\n---\nPeter Earle and Maximillian E. Novak",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-490,
			"y":7405,
			"width":380,
			"height":120
		},
		{
			"id":"40eb47c3ef08be5a",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"💵 That worldview where money is a measure of salute?\n---\nMoney really is the ultimate signifier...",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":430,
			"y":7525,
			"width":440,
			"height":140,
			"color":"6"
		},
		{
			"id":"31793240f96b9314",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"It's called \"networking\"",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-490,
			"y":6475,
			"width":260,
			"height":60,
			"color":"4"
		},
		{
			"id":"3df206418f34d8a5",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"So it usually goes with revolutions...",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1570,
			"y":4620,
			"width":400,
			"height":60,
			"color":"6"
		},
		{
			"id":"ef60b9e37b51d7da",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"So far\n---\nBut people learn...",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1370,
			"y":4760,
			"width":260,
			"height":60,
			"color":"2"
		},
		{"id":"d674c3e21ca88716","type":"text","text":"⭐ The Life of Daniel Defoe\n---\nIn a very condensed format.","x":-2180,"y":3860,"width":300,"height":200,"color":"0"},
		{"id":"d3b4516848b37f0d","type":"text","text":"⏰ Daniel Defoe was born in 1660\n---\nIt was a time of renewal, as Charles II restored the monarchy after a brief attempt at a progressive republic that devolved into a puritan military dictatorship.","x":-2470,"y":4180,"width":460,"height":200},
		{
			"id":"61c6472d86377400",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"📷 This guy?\n---\n\n\nYou can see it for yourself on <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Daniel_Defoe_Kneller_Style.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Wikimedia.\n<img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Daniel_Defoe_Kneller_Style.jpg/960px-Daniel_Defoe_Kneller_Style.jpg\" /></a>",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-3070,
			"y":4550,
			"width":260,
			"height":400
		},
		{
			"id":"5b4d451a709f0da1",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"👥 Daniel Defoe's family were London candle makers.\n---\nA successful bourgeois family.\nHis father was the first born in England from a puritan Flemish family fleeing religious persecution.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-2480,
			"y":4550,
			"width":480,
			"height":200
		},
		{
			"id":"6f30d97bbab96763",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"What kind of book are we talking about here?\n---\nHe studied the Great Atlases and the journals of merchant travelers of the times.\nHe kept up to date with scientific colonial exploration.\nHe also had an interest for practical knowledge manuals, which would later give his own writing some realism and depth.\nSome names come to mind...",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-3000,
			"y":6490,
			"width":420,
			"height":330
		},
		{
			"id":"458077cf65aea0f1",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"He loved to gather information.\n---\nThat was the key to a good deal.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-2680,
			"y":6870,
			"width":410,
			"height":120,
			"color":"6"
		},
		{
			"id":"6a3eb1ddad2c0ac6",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Did Daniel Defoe read any fiction?\n---\nHe was famously suspicious of fiction, that his religious upbringing pushed him to consider \"lies told for pleasure\".\n",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-2460,
			"y":7220,
			"width":540,
			"height":180
		},
		{
			"id":"c06caf1ce1c855b9",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Wait, how did he reconcile that with the fact that he literaly wrote fiction?\n---\nDefoe didn’t just ignore the contradiction; he built an entire philosophical defense for it. He called his method \"Religious Allegory\" or \"Parabolic Writing.\"",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1760,
			"y":7660,
			"width":520,
			"height":210,
			"color":"2"
		},
		{"id":"49209c0bf5486f14","type":"text","text":"I can't help but wonder if this psychological bias in stories reinforces a hyper-individualistic society.\n---","x":900,"y":3220,"width":300,"height":200,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"d0c1f86e10f949da","type":"text","text":"Robinson Crusoe?\n---\nRobinson Crusoe is an English adventure novel by Daniel Defoe, first published on 25 April 1719.\nMost people are familiar with its narrative of a sailor shipwrecked on a wild island.\nBut few people even know the story of the story.","x":-35,"y":3220,"width":300,"height":200,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"6a342d3d556dcaa3","type":"text","text":"What do you mean, the story of the story?\n---\nI mean the story of how the book came to be, and the story of its author.","x":-320,"y":2960,"width":300,"height":200,"color":"0"},
		{"id":"title","type":"text","text":"⭐ The true story of the story of Robinson Crusoe\n---","x":360,"y":2680,"width":300,"height":200,"color":"4"},
		{
			"id":"129c1ea38464bd60",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"I know...\n---\nIt's probably more than they deserve.\nIn fact this is precisely about getting more than one deserves.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1640,
			"y":3500,
			"width":260,
			"height":220,
			"color":"2"
		},
		{"id":"title_aside2","type":"text","text":"Though I guess a lot of them were white men.\n---\nSorry, its mostly their story.\n  But it doesn't have to be about them.","x":1400,"y":3200,"width":300,"height":200,"color":"0"},
		{
			"id":"c3f78645024410ce",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"I also think it's important to understand the world...\n---\nAnd where things come from.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-2720,
			"y":7020,
			"width":420,
			"height":145,
			"color":"2"
		},
		{
			"id":"4e956b014fce2d23",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"🚧 I'm sorry, the Inclosure story is another DLC.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-2160,
			"y":6960,
			"width":200,
			"height":133,
			"color":"3"
		},
		{
			"id":"bbebbd90befb593a",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"He really did like allegories...",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-2760,
			"y":7600,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"e7fb061c2668af1b",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"William Dampier",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1960,
			"y":8200,
			"width":260,
			"height":60,
			"color":"1"
		},
		{
			"id":"4aa765f37fcebc89",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"🚧 I'm sorry, Louis XIV is in another DLC",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-3030,
			"y":7580,
			"width":200,
			"height":133,
			"color":"3"
		},
		{
			"id":"041706c4eac2b33b",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Very much the rebel entrepreneur of the time",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-5295,
			"y":6118,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"27a1954a4a5e8183",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"With deep ties to politics...",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-5295,
			"y":6258,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"f9a85ef1f4484755",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"What kind of political intrigue?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-4955,
			"y":6358,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"37f8d8124e01bffb",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"political rebel/ problematic entrepreneur",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-5615,
			"y":6368,
			"width":260,
			"height":60,
			"color":"1"
		},
		{
			"id":"57ae2cb5f62f43eb",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"In 1685 he bore arms in Monmouth Rebellion",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-6090,
			"y":6480,
			"width":260,
			"height":60,
			"color":"1"
		},
		{
			"id":"f2c4a78c2f9975be",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Until he became a spy for the government!\n---\nThe Tory minister Robert Harley bailed him out of prison on condition that Daniel Defoe work for him.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-5310,
			"y":6672,
			"width":380,
			"height":230
		},
		{
			"id":"d377bddbf0439eaf",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"89 then he became close advisor to William of Orange\nCONNECTION TO 1701 THERE",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-6010,
			"y":6846,
			"width":460,
			"height":90,
			"color":"1"
		},
		{
			"id":"10818a63bbc83eb9",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Prison?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-5260,
			"y":6989,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"a8d38e0524f7896d",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"what kind of government",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-6030,
			"y":7209,
			"width":260,
			"height":60,
			"color":"1"
		},
		{
			"id":"674e6a3c3e3e61d0",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"then he was imprisoned in 1703",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-5610,
			"y":7216,
			"width":400,
			"height":80,
			"color":"1"
		},
		{
			"id":"9f04098fd76affe4",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"👥 Robert Harley",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-4970,
			"y":7063,
			"width":180,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"a331d00687a688d3",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Though the rest of his life would be full of political intrigue...",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-4620,
			"y":6428,
			"width":420,
			"height":110,
			"color":"4"
		},
		{
			"id":"b88844f76bf4c415",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"🏁 and thats the end of robinson crusoe",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-2810,
			"y":9381,
			"width":260,
			"height":60,
			"color":"1"
		},
		{
			"id":"e56458bd0df6f92f",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"defoe rest of life",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-3160,
			"y":9471,
			"width":260,
			"height":60,
			"color":"1"
		},
		{
			"id":"2e1ab5221c315e9d",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"🏁 end of defoe",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-3160,
			"y":9611,
			"width":260,
			"height":60,
			"color":"1"
		},
		{
			"id":"ff888cb0f93683c4",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"⭐ The story of copyright",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-4100,
			"y":8681,
			"width":260,
			"height":60,
			"color":"1"
		},
		{
			"id":"20daebf4571d973f",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"In Prison, he started his own private publication.\n---\nA newsletter if you will.\n<a href=\"https://archive.org/details/bub_gb_El8TAAAAQAAJ\" target=\"_blank\">\"A Review of the Affairs of France\"</a> started as a weekly chronicle that shifted according to Daniel Defoe's interests.\n<iframe src=\"https://archive.org/details/bub_gb_El8TAAAAQAAJ\"></iframe>",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-4715,
			"y":7083,
			"width":460,
			"height":267,
			"color":"4"
		},
		{
			"id":"5929c71a78c15ca1",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"🚧 He was instrumental in the redacting of the Act of Union in 1707\n---\nYou know, the creation of a \"United Kingdom\".\nBut this is a story for another DLC.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-5105,
			"y":7363,
			"width":225,
			"height":142,
			"color":"3"
		},
		{
			"id":"53e72cec6b7fa897",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Spying?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-4845,
			"y":6842,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"4ee260ef31d9900b",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"\"France?\" What does France have to do with it?\n---\nDefoe was a fervent admirer of Louis XIV's militaristic centralism.\nBy talking about France, he could criticize the English government with a veneer of deniability.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-3650,
			"y":7363,
			"width":490,
			"height":220
		},
		{
			"id":"5b9234d08f40366a",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"🗝️ In 1701, Daniel Defoe published The True-Born Englishman\n---\norange TBC with the contents\nhow famous was he? 41 yo",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-3720,
			"y":6752,
			"width":400,
			"height":180,
			"color":"1"
		},
		{
			"id":"05a22844cd0ac569",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"It was much pirated\n---\ngreen tbc content\nDefoe’s most famous work at the time was a satirical poem called _The True-Born Englishman_. It was a massive hit, but it became his biggest financial tragedy.\n\n- **The Theft:** While Defoe sold a few legitimate copies, pirate printers flooded the streets with cheap, one-penny versions.\n    \n- **The Loss:** Defoe later claimed that over **80,000 pirated copies** were sold on the streets of London. He didn’t receive a single farthing from those sales.\ndid he use the term pirate himself?  branch into the pirate hub",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-4200,
			"y":6933,
			"width":420,
			"height":430,
			"color":"1"
		},
		{
			"id":"15ffce56be6fb0f6",
			"type":"text",
			"text":" The True-Born Englishman\n itself",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-3420,
			"y":7020,
			"width":340,
			"height":145,
			"color":"1"
		},
		{
			"id":"c6af20895de1c73a",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"What was it before",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-4660,
			"y":8360,
			"width":260,
			"height":60,
			"color":"1"
		},
		{
			"id":"af6635b4e9d0d251",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"How did it compare to the one in the sea",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-4440,
			"y":8440,
			"width":260,
			"height":60,
			"color":"1"
		},
		{
			"id":"6bf4d15935fded99",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"🏴‍☠️ Around 1709, Daniel Defoe's \"Review\" turned its attention to the question of piracy\n---\nNo, not the one in the sea.\nUpset about his financial loss of opportunity cost in his previous experiences, he started claiming a bold new idea: a BOOK should be the AUTHOR’s Property.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-4450,
			"y":7940,
			"width":390,
			"height":300,
			"color":"4"
		},
		{
			"id":"f3f817ca4d964d3a",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"how was it received",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-4100,
			"y":8420,
			"width":260,
			"height":60,
			"color":"1"
		},
		{
			"id":"f033b3b0f313a483",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"After the Union Act, Daniel Defoe spent a lot of time in Edinburgh spying for the government.\n---\nHe monitored political dissent on the ground.\nAs the Union settled, he turned his attention to domestic affairs.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-4680,
			"y":7505,
			"width":390,
			"height":297,
			"color":"4"
		},
		{
			"id":"94da80804b693f8a",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"old man yelling at the clouds energy\n?? add meme",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-4260,
			"y":8600,
			"width":260,
			"height":60,
			"color":"1"
		},
		{
			"id":"c026b7ef76f5979a",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"1719 robinson crusoe published, lots of stuff in research",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-2880,
			"y":9080,
			"width":260,
			"height":55,
			"color":"1"
		},
